From 79b80934f3dc6b999876df0dbf0de0ee7d733a4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Wojciechowski <24755+wojo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:02:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GLM on CUDA: a kept state's disk image on one rank, its parts and where each byte sits in its lease

The rows store's view of a GLM kept state, without the store: the words (format,
position, head rows, ring bases, KDA copy bits), the KDA prefix, each DSA layer's
latent rows, scales and whole pools by position, its rings and pools in progress
as the state's own, the head's caches at a whole verify window (rows past the
head's own read as zeros), then the tail. Copies run a page of the lease at a
time. Nothing is wired to --learn-conversations yet.
---

